Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["The VC package", "Subsection"],

Cell["\<\
Estimation procedure by Ekkehart Schlicht (University of Munich). \
Implemented by Johannes Ludsteck (Institute for Employment Research \
Nuremberg).\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "VC is a method-of-moments estimation procedure for linear time series \
models with time-varying (random walk) coefficients, developed by Ekkehart \
Schlicht (University of Munich).\n\nConsider the model\n",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      \(y\_t = \(a\_t\) x\_t + u\_t\), "\n", 
      \(where\ \(a\_t\) and\ \(x\_t\) is\ are - vectors, \(u\_t\) 
        follows\ a\ normal\ distribution\ and\ \(a\_t\) 
        is\ generated\ by\ a\ random\ walk\ process\ of\ the\ form\), "\n", 
      \(a\_t = a\_\(t - 1\) + v\_t\), "\n", 
      \(where\ \(v\_t\) 
            follows\ a\ multivariate\ normal\ distribution\ with\ mean\ 0\ \
and\ variance - covariance\ matrix\ \[Sum] = 
        diag \(\((\[Sigma]\_1\%2,  ... , \[Sigma]\_n\%2)\)\(.\)\)\)}], "Text",
    
    FontFamily->"Times"],
  "\nIt is routine to estimate such models by Maximum Likelihood using the \
Kalman filter.  However, for short time series, maximum likelihood estimation \
produces corner solutions (",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Sigma]\_i\%2\)]],
  "=0) in many cases, even if the true variances are strictly positive. VC \
does better in many cases."
}], "Text",
  FontSize->14],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["This loads the package", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(<< VC`\)], "Input"],

Cell["Load some helper packages used to generate simulated data.", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(<< Statistics`ContinuousDistributions`;\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(<< Statistics`MultinormalDistribution`;\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(<< LinearAlgebra`MatrixManipulation`;\)\)}], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Two further helper functions. VCModel generates simulated data for \
a linear time series model with varying coefficients.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(\(VCModel[t_, Sigma_?MatrixQ, bv_?VectorQ, uv_, 
          opts___] := \[IndentingNewLine]Module[{n = Length[bv], mndist, 
            brand, urand, b, x, y, 
            bMat}, \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine]mndist = 
            MultinormalDistribution[Table[0.0, {n - 1}], 
              Sigma]; \[IndentingNewLine]brand := 
            Map[Random[NormalDistribution[0.0, #]] &, 
              Sqrt[bv]]; \[IndentingNewLine]urand := 
            RandomArray[NormalDistribution[0.0, Sqrt[uv]], 
              t]; \[IndentingNewLine]x = 
            Map[Join[{1.0}, #] &, 
              RandomArray[mndist, t]]; \[IndentingNewLine]b = 
            Flatten[bMat = 
                NestList[#1 + brand &, Table[1.0, {n}], 
                  t - 1]]; \[IndentingNewLine]y = 
            X[x] . b + urand; \[IndentingNewLine]{y, x, 
            Transpose[bMat]}];\)\(\[IndentingNewLine]\)
    \)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(X[x_] := 
        Module[{t, n}, \[IndentingNewLine]{t, n} = 
            Dimensions[
              x]; \[IndentingNewLine]SparseArray[{i_, j_} /; \((i - 1)\)\ n < 
                  j \[LessEqual] i\ n \[RuleDelayed] 
              x\[LeftDoubleBracket]i, 
                j - \((i - 1)\)\ n\[RightDoubleBracket], {t, 
              t\ n}]];\)\)}], "Input"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Here we set the parameters of the model and generate the data\
\>", \
"Subsubsection"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(SeedRandom[123]; t = 50;\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(S = 5 {{1, 0.5}, {0.5, 1}};\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(bv = {0.05, 0.1, 0.15};\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\({y, x, b} = VCModel[t, S, bv, 1.0];\)\)}], "Input"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["This is a plot of the time paths of the three coefficients", \
"Subsubsection"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Show[
      GraphicsArray[
        Map[ListPlot[#, \[IndentingNewLine]PlotJoined \[Rule] True, 
              DisplayFunction \[Rule] Identity] &, 
          b]], \[IndentingNewLine]DisplayFunction \[Rule] $DisplayFunction, 
      ImageSize \[Rule] 500]\)], "Input"],

Cell[GraphicsData["PostScript", "\<\
