Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
The next cell contains a call to VCEstimate. VCEstimate returns a \
List containing [1] a matrix with the time paths of the coefficients bhat, \
[2] a matrix with the respective standard errors sdb, [3] the standard error \
of the residual sdu, and [4] the vector of standard errors of the random walk \
residuals sdi. Since the computation of the estimates may be time-consuming \
for lage models, the estimation process is reported\
\>", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\({bhat, sdb, sdu, sdi} = VCEstimate[x, y];\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(VCEstimate::"conv" \(\(:\)\(\ \)\) 
      "Convergence achieved after \!\(2068\) iterations."\)], "Message"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The cell above serves as an iteration monitor. It prints the number \
of completed iterations, the actual value of the  convergence criterion and \
the actual value of variance ratios (=sdi/sdu). The convergence criterion \
used to compute the estimator is the maximum of relative changes of the \
variance ratios between two successive steps of the fixed point \
iteration.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
Iteration: 2000  Criterion: 0.0000120674
Variance Ratios: {0.00443499, 0.0190809, 0.0927226}\
\>", "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
CIPlot is a helper function which allows to plot the coefficients \
together with confidence interval bands (default option is 0.95 percent \
bands).\
\>", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Options[CIPlot]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({CILevel \[Rule] 0.95`, RegressorNames \[Rule] Automatic, 
      ImageSize \[Rule] 200, Columns \[Rule] 4}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(CIPlot[bhat, sdb, Columns \[Rule] 3]\)], "Input"],

