Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
If the option StoppingCriterion\[Rule]a is given, VCEstimate stops \
the fixed point interation if the maximum relative change of the variance \
ratios is  0.1^a (default value is StoppingCriterion\[Rule]5).\
\>", \
"Subsubsection"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\({bhat, sdb, sdu, sdi} = 
        VCEstimate[x, y, StoppingCriterion \[Rule] 3];\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(VCEstimate::"conv" \(\(:\)\(\ \)\) 
      "Convergence achieved after \!\(547\) iterations."\)], "Message"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The extension of VC to panel data is straightforward. This \
extension is implemented in the package. Since only less users will be \
interested in panel data applications, we do not demonstrate them here. The \
interested reader is referred to the package documentation (type \
?VCEstimate). Note that panel data are tractable only if the cross-section \
dimension and time dimension are small (less than 100).\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
Iteration: 500  Criterion: 0.0012171
Variance Ratios: {0.00622885, 0.0193836, 0.0937203}\
\>", "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
